A||N||2||286SE'S||T-Top installation..How difficult?||||5||
Z||000000||286SE'S||10-30-2001||10:39 AM||||There is an 84 SE with T-Tops at the junkyard<BR>Is it possible to cut the whole roof off with<BR>a portable saw and remove the rivited sections to install on another car?<BR>I was going to do a sun roof but when I sat in this car it remided me of my old X 1/9 with all the open space obove and loved it.<BR>Has anyone done this? Should it be left to a professional. I have read all the archives I could find and just found hints that it could be done. <BR>Thanks for any first hand information you have. Tell me what kind of saw is needed. The yard does not allow torches.<BR>Terry<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||gomobile||10-30-2001||03:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 286SE'S:<BR><B>There is an 84 SE with T-Tops at the junkyard<BR>Is it possible to cut the whole roof off with<BR>a portable saw and remove the rivited sections to install on another car?<BR>I was going to do a sun roof but when I sat in this car it remided me of my old X 1/9 with all the open space obove and loved it.<BR>Has anyone done this? Should it be left to a professional. I have read all the archives I could find and just found hints that it could be done. <BR>Thanks for any first hand information you have. Tell me what kind of saw is needed. The yard does not allow torches.<BR>Terry</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well I though about taking a project like that and after looking at the cost associated with it I said NOT worth it. I gather i am investing my $$$ internaly and externally (nicer rims and wheels). But, just in case here is web page you can look at for some inside info (good_luck).<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fierottop.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierottop.com/</A> <BR>||||reg||6
Z||000002||T-top Fiero||10-30-2001||07:41 PM||||Terry,<BR>I've done two T-top installs. One in my car and another in a fellow club members car. Both sets came from junkyard cars.<BR>The only problem now is that some replacement parts are nonexistant ie, door/glass weather strip & A & B pillar trim caps. <BR>If all the parts on the junkyard car are in good usable shape I say go for it. (I/we used a cordless reciprocating saw to cut the roof off.) If they are not it will not be worth your while.<P>Pat||||reg||1
